DZLL Community Source Licence v1.0

Copyright (c) Gareth Brown and DZLL contributors.

This licence applies to DZLL, also known as DayZ Linux Launcher, including its
source code, packaged releases, images, audio, icons, documentation, branding,
and other project materials, unless a file clearly states otherwise.

DZLL is made source-available so that the DayZ Linux community can inspect it,
audit it, learn from it, improve it, and use it safely. DZLL is intended to
remain free for players and the community. It must not be turned into a paid
product, paid service, advertising platform, paid server-promotion system, or
other monetised product.

1. Permission

Subject to the terms of this licence, you may:

a. use DZLL free of charge;

b. view, inspect, and audit the source code;

c. modify DZLL for personal, private, educational, or community use;

d. share unmodified copies of DZLL free of charge;

e. share modified copies or forks of DZLL free of charge, provided that you
   comply with this licence;

f. submit patches, pull requests, bug reports, translations, documentation, or
   other contributions to the DZLL project.

2. Non-Commercial Requirement

DZLL must remain free of charge.

You may not, directly or indirectly:

a. sell, rent, lease, license, sublicense, or charge for DZLL;

b. place DZLL, modified versions of DZLL, or access to DZLL behind a paywall,
   subscription, donation requirement, membership requirement, paid Discord role,
   paid Patreon tier, paid website account, or similar access restriction;

c. bundle DZLL with a paid product, paid launcher, paid mod pack, paid server
   package, paid hosting package, paid support package, or paid service;

d. use DZLL as part of a commercial service, hosted service, managed service,
   software-as-a-service offering, launcher service, server-listing service, or
   server-management service;

e. monetise DZLL through advertisements, affiliate links, referral links,
   sponsorships, paid placement, paid ranking, promoted servers, boosted server
   visibility, paid recommendations, paid search priority, or similar schemes;

f. charge server owners, communities, players, clans, groups, or any other party
   for inclusion in DZLL, visibility in DZLL, priority in DZLL, compatibility
   with DZLL, or support by DZLL;

g. use DZLL to collect payments, commissions, referral fees, server-promotion
   fees, listing fees, or other financial benefits connected to DayZ servers,
   mods, communities, or players;

h. remove this non-commercial requirement from DZLL or from any modified version
   or redistribution of DZLL.

This section does not prevent ordinary players, server owners, or communities
from using DZLL for free. A DayZ server or community may recommend DZLL to its
players, link to the official DZLL project, or help users install DZLL, provided
that DZLL itself is not sold, paywalled, bundled into a paid service, used for
paid placement, or otherwise monetised.

3. Attribution and Licence Notices

All copies, redistributions, modified versions, forks, packages, and substantial
portions of DZLL must include:

a. this licence;

b. the original copyright notice;

c. clear attribution to the original DZLL project;

d. a link or reference to the official DZLL project, where reasonably possible;

e. any notices required by third-party dependencies or assets.

You may not remove, obscure, falsify, or misrepresent DZLL copyright notices,
licence notices, attribution notices, or original project references.

4. Modified Versions and Forks

You may create and share modified versions or forks of DZLL free of charge,
provided that:

a. the modified version remains under this licence;

b. the modified version remains free of charge and non-commercial;

c. the modified version includes this licence and the required attribution;

d. the modified version clearly states that it has been modified;

e. the modified version clearly states that it is not an official DZLL release,
   unless it has been approved by the original DZLL maintainer;

f. the modified version does not mislead users about its origin, authorship,
   safety, endorsement, or relationship to the official DZLL project.

5. Branding, Names, and Logos

The DZLL name, DayZ Linux Launcher name, DZLL logos, icons, visual identity,
project identity, and other branding are part of the identity of the official
project.

You may not use DZLL branding in a way that:

a. falsely suggests that a modified version, fork, package, website, server list,
   service, or community is official;

b. falsely suggests endorsement, approval, partnership, or sponsorship by the
   original DZLL project or its maintainer;

c. confuses users about whether they are using the official DZLL release;

d. removes the original project identity from an official or unmodified
   redistribution;

e. uses DZLL branding to promote a paid product, paid service, paid server
   listing, paid server placement, advertisement, sponsorship, or other
   monetised activity.

Modified versions and forks must use clear naming, labelling, or visual
distinction so that users can tell they are not official DZLL releases.

6. Source Availability and Transparency

If you distribute a modified version of DZLL, you must make the corresponding
modified source code available under this licence at no charge.

The source code must be sufficient for users to inspect, audit, build, and
understand the modified version. You may not distribute a modified binary,
installer, package, or bundled version of DZLL without making the corresponding
modified source code available under the same terms.

7. Contributions

By submitting a contribution to DZLL, including code, documentation, assets,
translations, bug fixes, patches, pull requests, or other project materials, you
agree that your contribution may be included in DZLL and licensed under this
licence.

You confirm that you have the right to submit the contribution and that, to the
best of your knowledge, it does not knowingly infringe the rights of others.

8. Third-Party Components

DZLL may use third-party libraries, tools, assets, or dependencies. Those
third-party components remain subject to their own licences.

This licence does not grant rights to third-party materials beyond the rights
granted by their respective owners and licences.

